        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "HOML LABOUR VIEWS (Router) London, Juno 25:---\nThe General Council of the Trade Union Congress on the National Executive of the Labour Party at a joint meeting in London passed a resolution declaring that disgraceful working conditions in Chinese mills are the immediate cause of the present disturbance in China. The resolution expresses the opinion that immediate steps should be taken to carry out in the Treaty Ports the recommendations of the Shanghai Child Labour Commission and to assist the Chinese Government to give general effect to their recent factory act and raise the general conditions of Chinese workers. The extracerritorial regime is provocative and dangerous and should be ended as soon as possible by an international conference on British initiative. The proposed conference on Chinese tariffs gives the opportunity for such initiative in respect of the Treaty Ports.",
            "block_bbox": [
