        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "CHINA BONDS (Router) London, June 25:.... In the House of Commons replying to Sir. T. Bowater, Mr. A. M. Samuel, for Foreign Secretary, said that British Coupons of the Hukuang Railway is also 1911 had recently been paid. He was not at present in a position to make any statement with regard to the position of British holders of the Bonds of the German issue of this and other similar loans beyond giving an assurance that His Majesty's representative at Poking would continue to take every opportunity to press the Chinese Government to remedy the default.",
